# Campaign product notes — {{ company_name }}'s own automatic replies

## What to write here

The phrases {{ company_name }}'s own systems send back on their own: the
acknowledgement a ticket tool returns, the confirmation a form sends, the
out-of-office your team sets, the notice a shop or a switchboard mails after a
missed contact. Quote them the way they are actually sent — same wording, same
language — one per line, with a word on which system sends each.

Add anything else that arrives in a campaign thread and is not a person:
delivery receipts, bounce notices, no-reply senders.

-
-

## Why it matters

`/cs-campaign-tick` classifies every reply that lands after an outreach mail. It
already knows the generic openers ("request received", "out of office"); what it
cannot guess is the wording that is specific to you. An automatic
acknowledgement it does not recognise reads exactly like a human answering — the
contact is marked engaged, the campaign stops following up, and the real reply
that never came is never waited for.
